(1) one pass from the deepest level up, 20000 multisets of 2..14 elements on [81, 243, 729, 135, 405, 675, 2025, 945, 1575, 4725, 625, 3125, 1323, 3465, 10395, 23625]: the levels deleted are exactly the levels contractible for B itself; no contractible level is left; the group left is prod p^(r_p): no exception
(2) Z_9, B = {0, 3, 7}: digit of index 0 takes [0, 1], digit of index 1 takes [0, 1, 2] on the support; level 1 contractible True, level 2 contractible True; signings (first +): +++ sum 3 good True, ++- sum 1 good True, +-+ sum 1 good True, +-- sum -1 good True
(3) 5000 multisets of 2..8 elements with no full group at any level of any tree, 115716 signings: good exactly when the sum is not 0 (94700 good); for 751 of the multisets the hypothesis of Proposition 4 of the first result fails (some digit takes every value on the support)
